{
  "id": "Compound::DB00331 - Gene::4715",
  "verbalization": "Metformin is shown to interact with Ndufb9 through a shared pathway involving Nadh Dehydrogenase (ubiquinone) or (quinone) Activity. The evidence suggests that Metformin binds to Ndufa12 or Ndufv3, which are subunits of the Nadh Dehydrogenase complex, and that this binding leads to participation in the activity of Ndufb9. This indicates that Metformin may modulate the function of Ndufb9 through the regulation of the Nadh Dehydrogenase complex. The high scores in all three paths suggest a consistent and robust mechanistic link, with Metformin acting as a modulator of the complex that includes Ndufb9. The presence of multiple binding sites and the involvement of different Nduf subunits in the same pathway support the idea that Metformin influences Ndufb9 through a pathway that is central to mitochondrial respiration. The integration of these findings highlights a potential mechanism by which Metformin may exert its therapeutic effects on Ndufb9, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct interaction and functional impact.",
